  "behavior": [
    "IndexedMapNode uses actual flat MapLinkNode, K, i32 fields; IndexedDataMapNode uses MapLinkNode, ManuallyDrop<V>, ManuallyDrop<K>, i32. Only the actual link prefix is borrowed/cast; no whole Rust MapNode/DataMapNode/ListValueNode projection spans native reused padding.",
    "Flat fields match pinned GCC node size/alignment/key/value/index offsets in all ten measured equivalent scalar/align32 payload cases. Seven formerly differing rows now agree.",
    "The shared map_payload helper constructs value before key, cleans value if key construction fails, and destroys key before value including Rust panic cleanup. Allocation precedes construction through the existing NativeNodeOwner substrate.",
    "Existing key/value mutation, signed Index extremes, successor preservation, copy failure and owner/callback Drop-panic behavior remain covered by the original eighteen native rows and fourteen focused lifetime tests.",
    "Native placement allocations report the actual requested bytes through a named LayoutArena. Rust typed node size and adjacent allocation spacing in a warmed incremental arena equal these bytes for each of ten rows. Initial fresh-arena alignment reserve is excluded explicitly; backing allocator overhead is not claimed identical."
  ],
