  "native_probe_adaptation": "GCC -std=c++17 -fno-access-control exposes exact pinned nested types. Named LayoutArena records placement Allocate request and supplies 32-byte aligned backing storage so over-aligned construction is defined. It rounds physical backing bytes independently; requested bytes are reported before rounding.",
  "generic_payload_abi_scope": "Measured x86_64 Linux GCC13.3 versus Rust1.98.1. Payload equivalence requires matching payload size/alignment/layout: u8, i32 and repr(C,align(32)) one-byte member with sizeof32. This does not establish universal cross-language generic ABI. C++ empty objects occupy at least one byte while Rust ZSTs may occupy zero; explicit representation adapters remain needed for native byte equality there.",
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "Typed IndexedMap still uses simplified IndexedNode/Vec buckets; IndexedDataMap still separates keys and values. Container canonical storage, allocation count, callback observation and outstanding class-method parity are not claimed closed.",
    "Arbitrary address-sensitive C++ construction, move/assignment side effects, C++ throwing-noexcept destruction, platform-specific ABI and arbitrary mapped payload ABI remain outside this measured domain.",
    "Historical standalone node receipt remains constructor/lifetime evidence; historical layout-gap receipt remains a record of the pre-correction mismatch. This receipt supersedes only its ten measured indexed layouts."
